<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Better Traders Guild - Utility Mech Dorm Duty

    BTG_MechDorm: the resting duty for utility mechs that have no work behaviour yet
    (Lifter, Fabricor). Instead of pacing their room forever (the old BTG_WanderInArea
    wander), they park against a wall of the room they were spawned into and dormant
    self-charge, reading as docked equipment. The room is resolved def-agnostically by
    rect membership (HomeRoomArea), the same model the cleansweeper uses.

    Priority order:
    1. Return home - walk back into the home room if combat self-defense or player
       interference displaced the mech, so the node below always parks it in its own
       room.
    2. Dorm - park on a wall-adjacent, non-door-flanking cell (MechIdlePark) and
       dormant self-charge (SelfShutdown, forceSleep off; the job expiry re-walks this
       tree ~every 250 ticks, so future work nodes added above will wake it).

    If lifters/fabricors grow real duties later (hauling, crafting), their job-giver
    nodes slot in above the return-home node, exactly like the cleansweeper and
    agrihand trees.

    Used by: LordJob_MechDorm, assigned via RoomMechLordHelper (behavior=Dorm) to the
    Lifter (RoomPart Mech_Lifter) and Fabricor (RoomPart Mech_Fabricor).
  -->

  <DutyDef>
    <defName>BTG_MechDorm</defName>
    <thinkNode Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <!-- 1. Displaced (combat, player interference): walk back into the home room. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGMechDormReturnHome" />
        <!-- 2. Park against a room wall and dormant self-charge. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGMechDormStandby" />
      </subNodes>
    </thinkNode>
  </DutyDef>

</Defs>
